==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*kaðʲa-||to leave}}. Cognates are found in almost every Uralic language, e.g. {{cog|se|guođđit||to leave something, to depart}}, {{cog|sms|kue´đđed||to leave smth}}, {{cog|mdf|кадомс||to leave}}, {{cog|chm|кодаш||to stay}}, {{cog|udm|кыльыны||to stay}}, {{cog|hu|hagy||to let, to leave}}, {{cog|mns|хули||to leave}}, {{cog|sel|||to leave|tr=/quəčə-/}}. Labialization of the stem vowel occurred in Proto-Finnic, compare {{cog|et|kadu||loss}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyphenation|ka|to|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑto|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑto]}}

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[failure|Failure]] of [[crop]]s.
# [[loss|Loss]], [[disappearance]], [[lack]]; used primarily in compound terms.
#: ''[[yleisö]]'''kato''''' = lack or loss of audience

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-valo|ka|t|d|o|a}}

=====Derived terms=====
* verbs: [[kadota]]

=====Compounds=====
* [[katokorvaus]]
* [[katovahinko]]
* [[katovuosi]]
* [[kulmakarvakato]]
* [[silmäripsikato]]
* [[yleisökato]]

===Etymology 2===
A dialectal or colloquial 2nd person imperative present of {{m|fi|katsoa||to look}}. The corresponding infinitive is {{m|fi|kattoa}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyphenation|ka|to|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑto|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑtoˣ]}}

====Verb====
{{head|fi|verb form}}

# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[look]]!
#: '''''Kato''', tuolla on George!'' &mdash; ''Look, there's George!''
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[see]] (used often with [[nyt|ny]])
#: '''''Kato''' ny, mähän sanoin.'' &mdash; ''See, I told you so.''

=====Synonyms=====
* [[katso]]

====Interjection====
{{fi-int}}

# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[see]] or [[look]].
#* ''Se on '''kato''' sillä lailla.''
#** '''''See''', that’s the way it is.''
#* '''''Kato''' nääs!'' or '''''Kato kato!'''''
#** Literally: ''Look, look!.'' Uttered in surprise, not necessarily telling anyone to look anywhere.
#* ''...'''kato''' nääs.'' or ''...'''kato.'''''
#** ''...you see.'' (At the end of a sentence)

=====Synonyms=====
* [[katsos]], [[näet]], [[nimittäin]]

===See also===
* [[niinku]]
* [[nääs]]
* [[tiäksä]]

===Anagrams===
* [[kota#Finnish|kota]], [[toka#Finnish|toka]]

